*************************************************************
*V1-11
- Fix REL-2470 where:
     getDbInfoT(dbTop, OBSERVE_CAR ".IVAL", dummy,DBF_LONG,&lVal);
  was using the wrong OBSERVE_CAR output. It was changed to: 
     getDbInfoT(dbSadTop, OBSERVE_CAR ".VAL", dummy, DBF_STRING, carVAL);


*V1-10
DC2:

- fix getDbCaInfo.c such that it releases Channel Access connections after using them
  (this is the "channel access leak" impacting the TCS and DC2
- fix the cctop name in nirsTop.sch so that the camera can be correctly read from the cc.
- for the astCtx genSub, set the type for VALB and VALC to STRING so that the Track Frame 
  and Equinox values read from the TCS can be used internally
- remove links to non-existent records in the sysCar schematic
- resolve a problem where the top level CAR went IDLE-BUSY-IDLE rather than BUSY-IDLE when observations 
  were sequenced from the seqexec ... this caused the seqexec to skip steps
- improve the loading of CA connections from the TCS and A&G at bootup.

DC1:
- changed the dhs connection code to not connect to the DHS automatically at bootup.
  This removes a primary cause for DHS connection instability after reboots.
- changed shell prompt to say DC1

*V1-91 AWE
- This is the head of the repository before development work on V1-10.
- V1-9 was released (see CR-10 0813) but not tagged
- I think that this is consistent with the release directory V1-9.
- the main change in this version is the top level name in order to support
  the use of an alias gateway.
- There was also a variety of code that had not been checked into CVS and was thus missing.
  It has all been tracked down and checked in as of this tag

*V1-8:
- WCS automated loading for input files depending on camera,
  AO-fold and ISS port. Adheres to new WCS ICD as of November 2010.

--Starting GNIRS north DC RELEASE.NOTES
